{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310593,"nonce":"7RUrXDnp8rPkjm/mayiRsV1RNjg=","title":"`{}` always parses as an empty BLOCK, so an empty anonymous structure silently has no value. Breaks haxe.rtti.Meta.getType. Fix is a ...","message":"**`{}` in value position silently produces nothing.**\n\n```haxe\nvar o = {};                      // unused -\u003e \"works\" only because it is dead code\nvar o = {}; trace(\"\" + o);       // prints NOTHING, exit 0\nvar o:Dynamic = {}; o.a = 1;     // prints NOTHING, exit 0\nstatic function f():Dynamic { return {}; }   // W0020 cannot compile `f`;\n                                             // \"return type Ptr(Void) but\n                                             //  encountered Return with no value\"\nvar o = {a:1}; trace(o.a);       // 1   -- NON-empty is fine\n```\n\nMIR for the return case is unambiguous — the literal vanished entirely:\n\n```\nfn @M.f [name=f]() -\u003e *void {\n  bb0:\n    ret void          \u003c-- signature says *void\n}\n```\n\n**Root cause.** `parser/src/rd/expr.rs`, `parse_block_or_object` (~line 1478):\n\n```rust\n// Empty braces = empty block\nif peek(0) == LBrace \u0026\u0026 peek(1) == RBrace {\n    return Ok(Expr { kind: ExprKind::Block(Vec::new()), .. });\n}\n```\n\n`{}` is ALWAYS an empty block. An empty block has no value, so any use of the\nexpression yields nothing. `lower_object_literal` is never reached — this is not\na lowering bug, and the empty case in `lower_object_literal` is fine.\n\nRuled out on the way: empty string constants work (`var s = \"\"` -\u003e `len=0`), and\nit is not return-position parsing — `var x = {}; return x;` fails identically.\n\n\n`parse_block_or_object` is reached from expression position, but empty braces\nalso appear as `if (c) {}`, `while (c) {}`, `try {} catch ...`, and a bare `{}`\nstatement, where an empty BLOCK is the correct reading. Flipping the branch\nwithout establishing which callers are value-position would silently turn every\nempty block in the codebase into an object literal. Haxe itself resolves this in\ntyping rather than parsing.\n\n**Impact:** breaks `haxe.rtti.Meta.getType`, whose body is\n`return (meta == null || meta.obj == null) ? {} : meta.obj;` — this is the\nSIGSEGV family the conformance workflow labelled \"haxe.rtti.Meta.getType fails\nto lower\" (Issue10041, Issue5757).\n\n\n\nThe parser is RIGHT to yield `ExprKind::Block([])` for `{}`: upstream's parser\ndoes the same, and upstream's TYPER rewrites `EBlock []` in a value position\ninto `EObjectDecl []` (typer.ml `| EBlock [] when with_type \u003c\u003e NoValue`). So the\nfix is in the TAST lowering, not `parse_block_or_object`:\n`lower_value_expression` (expr/mod.rs) lowers an empty Block as `Object(vec![])`\nat the value positions — var/final initialiser, `return`, call argument. A\nstatement `{}` (if/else body) stays a block.\nEvidence: Issue9026 (`var key = {}`; `map[key] = 20; eq(20, map.get(key))`) —\nMIR had NO objectmap_set calls and `map.get(key)` = `const 0`; it PASSED before\nD10 only by the raw-value luck, then read `20 != \u003caddress\u003e`. Probes `mi_l`,\n`i9026`, `mi_k2`.\n\nLanded with two companions the change exposed: 73a5f8e0 (a `Null\u003cscalar\u003e` box\ninto an erased `T` formal at a CROSS-MODULE call is unboxed — the harness's\ninherited `unit.Test.eq`) and 71d7fded (an anonymous object boxed for Dynamic is\ntagged `TYPE_ANON_OBJECT`=6, so `Reflect.field(d, ..)` on a `Dynamic`-typed object\nno longer reads the box — `var d:Dynamic\u003cInt\u003e = {a:1}; Reflect.field(d,\"a\")` had\nSIGSEGV'd, pre-existing). Battery 433 -\u003e 437 (Issue12239, Issue2963, Issue3845 +\nflake), 0 lost; Issue5226 moved WRONG_ANSWER -\u003e COMPILE_FAIL on an abstract\nproperty WRITE (`f.hasFrom = 20`, the known\n[[bugs-abstract-properties-need-setter-writeback]] defect). Issue9026 STILL reads an\naddress in harness form only: the inherited `eq` goes through VIRTUAL dispatch\n(`virtual_dispatch.rs`), whose argument loop applies no coercion — FIXED 8ffd3a8c: the inherited `eq` takes resolved_method.rs's PARENT-CHAIN path, which had\nno coercion; the erased-formal rule is now one helper on direct/indirect/virtual and the\nid-keyed twin (reading a LOCAL callee's signature too) on both resolved-method paths.\nIssue9026 PASS in harness form; battery 438 -\u003e 439 (+Issue7428).\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_empty_object_literal_is_parsed_as_a_block` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}